---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Getting Started - Accessible UI Kit">
  <main id="main-content" class="docs-page">
    <article class="docs-content">
      <h1>Getting Started</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Start using accessible components in minutes. No build step required.
      </p>

      <section id="installation" aria-labelledby="installation-heading">
        <h2 id="installation-heading">Installation</h2>

        <h3>Option 1: Copy & Paste (Recommended)</h3>
        <p>
          The simplest way to use these components. Just copy the HTML and CSS from any component page
          and paste it into your project.
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li>Browse the <a href="/components">Components</a> catalog</li>
          <li>Click on a component to view its documentation</li>
          <li>Copy the HTML and CSS code snippets</li>
          <li>Paste into your project</li>
          <li>Customize the CSS variables to match your design</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>Option 2: Download the CSS</h3>
        <p>
          Download the complete CSS file with all components and tokens:
        </p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <pre><code>&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.example.com/accessible-ui-kit/1.0.0/styles.css"&gt;</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>
          <em>Note: CDN coming soon. For now, use Option 1.</em>
        </p>

        <h3>Option 3: Clone the Repository</h3>
        <p>
          For full access to source files, tests, and documentation:
        </p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <pre><code class="language-bash">git clone https://github.com/your-org/accessible-ui-kit.git
cd accessible-ui-kit
pnpm install
pnpm dev</code></pre>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="design-tokens" aria-labelledby="tokens-heading">
        <h2 id="tokens-heading">Design Tokens</h2>
        <p>
          All components use CSS custom properties (variables) for consistent styling.
          Include the tokens file to enable theming:
        </p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <pre><code class="language-css" set:html={`/* Add to your CSS or include tokens.css */
:root {
  /* Colors */
  --color-primary: #0066cc;
  --color-primary-hover: #0052a3;
  --color-text-primary: #111827;
  --color-background: #ffffff;

  /* Spacing */
  --space-sm: 0.5rem;
  --space-md: 1rem;
  --space-lg: 1.5rem;

  /* Typography */
  --font-family-sans: system-ui, sans-serif;
  --font-size-md: 1rem;

  /* And more... see tokens documentation */
}`} /></pre>
        </div>
        <p>
          <a href="/tokens">View all design tokens →</a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="dark-mode" aria-labelledby="dark-mode-heading">
        <h2 id="dark-mode-heading">Dark Mode</h2>
        <p>
          Dark mode is built-in. Add <code>data-theme="dark"</code> to your <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> element:
        </p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <pre><code class="language-html">&lt;html data-theme="dark"&gt;
  ...
&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>
          Or detect user preference automatically:
        </p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <pre><code class="language-javascript" set:html={`// Check user preference
const prefersDark = window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches;
document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', prefersDark ? 'dark' : 'light');`} /></pre>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="accessibility" aria-labelledby="a11y-heading">
        <h2 id="a11y-heading">Accessibility Guidelines</h2>
        <p>
          Every component follows these accessibility principles:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Semantic HTML:</strong> Uses correct elements (<code>&lt;button&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code>, etc.)</li>
          <li><strong>Keyboard navigation:</strong> All interactive elements work with keyboard only</li>
          <li><strong>Focus visibility:</strong> Clear focus indicators on all focusable elements</li>
          <li><strong>Screen reader support:</strong> Proper ARIA attributes where needed</li>
          <li><strong>Color contrast:</strong> Meets WCAG AA standards (4.5:1 for text)</li>
          <li><strong>Motion:</strong> Respects <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> preference</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <a href="/accessibility">Read our full accessibility guidelines →</a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="browser-support" aria-labelledby="browser-heading">
        <h2 id="browser-heading">Browser Support</h2>
        <p>
          Components support all modern browsers:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Chrome / Edge (last 2 versions)</li>
          <li>Firefox (last 2 versions)</li>
          <li>Safari (last 2 versions)</li>
          <li>iOS Safari (last 2 versions)</li>
          <li>Android Chrome (last 2 versions)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We use only stable CSS features. No experimental APIs or polyfills required.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="next-steps" aria-labelledby="next-heading">
        <h2 id="next-heading">Next Steps</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/components">Browse components</a></li>
          <li><a href="/components/button">Start with the Button component</a></li>
          <li><a href="/accessibility">Learn about accessibility</a></li>
          <li><a href="/eco-design">Understand eco-design principles</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .docs-page {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .docs-content h1 {
    font-size: var(--font-size-4xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .docs-content section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .docs-content h2 {
    font-size: var(--font-size-2xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    padding-top: var(--space-lg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .docs-content section:first-of-type h2 {
    border-top: none;
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .docs-content h3 {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .docs-content p {
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .docs-content ul, .docs-content ol {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    padding-left: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .docs-content li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
  }

  .code-block {
    margin: var(--space-md) 0;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .code-block pre {
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--space-md);
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .code-block code {
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    background: transparent;
    padding: 0;
  }
</style>
